retchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>⏞</mo></mover></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathsize=\"1.2em\"><mtext>Linear approximation</mtext></mstyle></mrow></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mphantom><mo>≈</mo></mphantom></mrow><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace></mstyle><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace></mstyle><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\"><munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>y</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⋅</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⏟</mo></munder></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathsize=\"1.2em\"><mtext>Quadratic part</mtext></mstyle></mrow></munder><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Now, we compute the terms of our Taylor polynomial.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Calculating the value of the function, we have\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" disp